"""{{ package_name }}.models — structured data contracts.

This package defines application models using Pydantic. These models serve as
the canonical representation of inputs, outputs, and domain data.

Each model marks an intentional boundary between user input, system logic,
and serialization. They should remain pure, side-effect free, and declarative.

- Pure: the same input always produces the same output
- Side-effect free: they don't modify anything outside themselves
- Declarative: they describe structure, not behavior

What does it mean to "define a boundary"?
A model separates concerns by drawing a line between:
- messy, unstructured user input
- safe, validated data used within your application
- structured output for serialization or APIs

It marks the point where data becomes trustworthy.
Think of it as an airlock: raw input goes in, validated data comes out.
